    <Element Type="Comment" Id="F7D3D729">
        <Comment>
            Game Rules and Conduct
            1. Winning is the Goal:
            All actions taken in the game must be in service of trying to win. Creativity and resourcefulness are encouraged--even if that includes abusing game mechanics or bugs.
            2. Exploits and Bugs:
            Using bugs, exploits, or any in-game mechanics to your advantage is allowed, as long as your intent is to win. 
            This does not include bugs that crash the game or softlock other players--those are considered trolling.
            3. Prohibited Behavior:
            The following behaviors are not allowed, as they go against the spirit of the game:
                Trolling: Intentionally derailing or disrupting the game without a genuine attempt to win, or deliberately trying to ruin the enjoyment of other players.
                This does not include legitimate gameplay such as attacking, defeating, or outplaying someone--even if they don&apos;t enjoy it.
                Kingmaking: Deliberately helping another player win when you no longer have a path to victory, instead of pursuing your own best possible outcome.
               This includes feeding resources, surrendering territory, or otherwise playing to benefit another player at your own competitive expense.
                Ragequitting: Especially when it involves intentionally destroying your own units, assets, or position before leaving the game. If you must leave, do so cleanly--don&apos;t sabotage the game for others
                AFK / Inactivity: Going idle or pretending to play while making no real effort to win is not allowed. If you can&apos;t continue playing, leave the game so that AI can take over. Remaining in-game while inactive prevents others from progressing and ruins the flow of play.
            Play to win--anything else is off-limits.
        </Comment>
    </Element>
