    <Element Type="Comment" Id="919276D7">
        <Comment>
            &lt;s val=&quot;AB_Description&quot;&gt;
            The Tau Empire once turned to AI development to bring order and progress. 
            But the AI revolt nearly destroyed them, throwing their society into chaos.
            Against all odds, the Tau defeated the machines and restored control, but the cost was profound.
            In the aftermath, the Tau rejected all forms of AI and machines, fearing another rebellion.
            The Ethereals assumed greater power, and the Greater Good became a rigid, dogmatic system, enforced through totalitarian rule.
            The Tau, now fearful of technology, abandoned their forward-thinking ideals.
            Ironically, in their effort to avoid becoming like the Imperium of Man, the Tau became it.
            The once-idealistic empire, driven by cooperation and unity, had transformed into an oppressive, bureaucratic regime.
            Their victory in the galaxy came at the cost of their freedom, and the Greater Good was now a cold, inflexible doctrine, enforced with unquestioning loyalty.
            The Tau ruled the stars, but the light of hope had dimmed.
            In the end, the Greater Good had become a grimdark system, defined by fear and stagnation, leaving the Tau to rule as the very empire they once swore to defeat.
            &lt;/s&gt;
        </Comment>
        <SubFunctionType Type="SubFuncType" Library="Ntve" Id="BF750C3C"/>
