        <Comment>
            &lt;s val=&quot;AB_Description&quot;&gt;
            The Necron dynasties, once fractured and dormant, now rise united beneath the gaze of the Silent King. 
            Their enemies are gone--swept aside by the cold, methodical wrath of an ancient race reclaiming its birthright. Tomb worlds blaze to life across the stars, casting the galaxy in cold, sovereign light.
            But this is not a victory of conquest alone.
            Szarekh does not seek dominion for its own sake. His is a higher purpose: to undo the sins of biotransference and restore the Necrontyr to their mortal form.
            With the galaxy subdued, his great work begins. Vaults are opened. Forbidden sciences stir. Hope--forgotten for millions of years--flickers once more.
            The curse of cold immortality may yet be broken. The Necrons, once rulers of death, now march toward life.
            A new age begins--not of metal, but of memory.
            &lt;/s&gt;
        </Comment>
        <SubFunctionType Type="SubFuncType" Library="Ntve" Id="BF750C3C"/>
