    <Element Type="Comment" Id="BDCF57F9">
        <Comment>
            &lt;s val=&quot;AB_Description&quot;&gt;
            The stars are silent. The last of the living have fallen, and the Necrons reign unchallenged. Under Imotekh the Stormlord, the galaxy has been subdued through relentless logic and unyielding war. Planets kneel beneath tomb monoliths. All resistance has been erased.
            But with the galaxy conquered, the curse awakens.
            The Flayer Virus spreads--not as infection, but as fate. With no flesh left to harvest, the hunger festers. Once-noble lords now claw at their own forms. Legions turn on themselves in spasms of madness.
            Imotekh watches with unblinking contempt. He purges what he must. He enforces order. He pretends. But the hunger will come for him too, in time.
            And so the stars endure, not in glory, but in silence. The galaxy is his. The war is won. But the enemy was never the living.
            The enemy... was time.
            &lt;/s&gt;
        </Comment>
