    <Element Type="Comment" Id="0F3AFAD6">
        <Comment>
            &lt;s val=&quot;AB_Description&quot;&gt;&lt;c val=&quot;F4FA29&quot;&gt;The galaxy has become little more than a playground.
            Caught in endless conflict--humans warring with Necrons, Tau clashing with the Imperium, Tyranids consuming all in their path--none noticed as Chaos crept in, unseen and unchecked. 
            One by one, the great powers fell, not with honor, but with laughter echoing behind them.
            Terra now festers as a grotesque parody of the God-Emperor&apos;s dream,
            its throne a monument to decay and mockery. The stars bleed, reality frays, and the Warp spills into all things.
            But there is no final victory. No dominion.
            The Ruinous Powers care not for peace or rulership.
            They revel in the suffering, in the madness, in the dance of endless strife. Even in triumph, they turn on one another, locked in their eternal, senseless war.
            In the end, everything serves only as a diversion for the forces of Chaos.
            And in the dark between stars, there is only the laughter of thirsting gods.&lt;/c&gt;&lt;/s&gt;
        </Comment>
