    <Element Type="Comment" Id="326202D8">
        <Comment>
            &lt;s val=&quot;AB_Description&quot;&gt;
            The Imperium has endured its darkest age--and emerged united beneath the banner of its last loyal son. Roboute Guilliman, Primarch of Ultramar, has cast down the pretenders and the old regime alike. 
            The High Lords of Terra lie broken, their corruption purged. Even the Lion, noble yet misguided, could not stand against Guilliman&apos;s relentless vision for the Imperium&apos;s rebirth.
            Now, from the Golden Throne to the edge of the Segmentum Obscurus, the Imperium stands as one.
            Gone are the days of fractured command and blind worship. In their place stands a new order--ruthless in purpose, absolute in discipline. The Imperial Creed is reshaped. 
            The bureaucracy is reforged in the image of Ultramar. Guilliman rules not as a god, but as a statesman, a general, a builder of empires.
            Mankind has not been saved. It has been commanded to endure.
            In the end, it was not faith that secured the future, but will. Not miracles, but order.
            The Age of the Primarch has begun.
            &lt;/s&gt;
        </Comment>
    </Element>
