        <Comment>
            &lt;s val=&quot;AB_Description&quot;&gt;
            The Age of Doubt has ended. The Imperium endures--not through diplomacy or faith, but through the sword.
            Roboute Guilliman lies defeated, his vision of unity shattered by the relentless judgment of his brother. The High Lords of Terra have been cast down, their decadence paid for in blood.
            From the shadows, the Lion has taken command.
            His Imperium does not speak in sermons or proclamations. It whispers through informants, it watches through unseen eyes. Order is not given--it is enforced.
            No rebellion stirs. No heresy survives.
            A galaxy once torn by division now kneels beneath a silent guardian. The Lion does not demand worship. He demands obedience. And under his reign, the Imperium knows peace--not out of hope, but out of fear.
            The throne is not warm. But it is finally secure.
            &lt;/s&gt;
        </Comment>
