    <Element Type="Comment" Id="774BDB3D">
        <Comment>
            &lt;s val=&quot;AB_Description&quot;&gt;
            The Hive Fleets, drawn from the depths of space, arrived as an unstoppable force, each fleet distinct in its purpose. 
            But even within the swarm, division emerged. Kraken, born from the deepest hunger, turned upon its kin in its insatiable drive for dominance.
            Leviathan and Jormungandr, once powerful forces in their own right, were consumed by Kraken&apos;s relentless will. 
            Neither size nor strategy could match Kraken&apos;s evolving swarm. The mighty fleets were devoured, their biomass absorbed, 
            and their tactics assimilated into Kraken&apos;s growing hunger.
            With its supremacy over the other Hive Fleets secured, Kraken turned its attention to the galaxy itself.
            The Imperium, once proud and vast, could not withstand the might of the swarm. The armies of mankind fell not through battle, but through total annihilation. 
            Each world, each colony, stripped of life, reduced to husks. The Imperial war machine crumbled, helpless against an enemy that adapted faster than they could respond.
            The Tau, ever sure of their &quot;Greater Good,&quot; faltered and perished. Their fleets, once swift and advanced, were overwhelmed, 
            their colonies wiped clean, their societies dismantled as the swarm consumed all.
            Even the Necrons, with all their ancient power and immortality, were not immune. The tomb worlds fell silent as Kraken&apos;s relentless hunger tore through the Necron legions, 
            reducing their once indomitable machines into organic fuel, their crypts nothing but abandoned relics of a forgotten era.
            Now, the galaxy is silent. There are no cries of resistance. No forces rising to challenge the swarm. 
            The stars that once burned brightly have been reduced to cold, lifeless remnants. The Hive Mind, having consumed all, rests.
            The galaxy is nothing more than sustenance. Its defenders, nothing more than fuel. Kraken reigns--not by conquest, but by the inevitability of hunger.
            &lt;/s&gt;
        </Comment>
    </Element>
