        <Comment>
            &lt;s val=&quot;AB_Description&quot;&gt;
            The Leviathan Hive Fleet has descended upon the galaxy, its vast aerial forces raining bio-plasmic fire from above. With overwhelming firepower and surgical precision, it annihilates all who stand in its path.
            There is no swarm--only the relentless fury of Leviathan&apos;s skyborne might.
            Kraken and Jormungandr, once feared for their monstrous fleets, fall before its supremacy. Their ships are shattered, their biomass absorbed into Leviathan&apos;s ever-growing hunger.
            The Imperium burns. Cities are reduced to rubble. Fleets collapse beneath relentless bombardment. Entire worlds vanish in silence, consumed by the storm from above.
            The Tau, armed with advanced technology and tactical precision, are outmaneuvered and wiped from existence. Their colonies, once beacons of progress, lie in ruin.
            Even the Necrons, ancient and undying, are not spared. Their tomb worlds, thought eternal, are turned to ash under Leviathan&apos;s fire.
            The galaxy, once defiant and alive, now lies broken and still.
            Leviathan reigns--not through numbers, but through unmatched aerial dominance.
            Its hunger is eternal. Its purpose, absolute. Its gaze now turns to the stars beyond.
            &lt;/s&gt;
        </Comment>
