    <Element Type="Comment" Id="45ED682E">
        <Comment>
            &lt;s val=&quot;AB_Description&quot;&gt;
            The Age of Unity has dawned. The Imperium, once fractured and bleeding, now stands resolute beneath the combined strength of two of its greatest sons. 
            Roboute Guilliman and Lion El&apos;Jonson, once adversaries driven by differing visions, have set aside their differences and forged a new, unbreakable alliance.
            Together, they have cast down the remnants of a corrupt and outdated order. The High Lords of Terra, with their decadence and disarray, have been swept away, 
            and their empire remade in the image of their righteous strength. The Lion&apos;s silent, unyielding will and Guilliman&apos;s unrelenting strategy have driven the forces of rebellion into the dark corners of the galaxy, 
            where they will not dare rise again.
            The Imperium stands united, its war machine unstoppable and its bureaucracy restructured to function as a singular, efficient whole. 
            The Galaxy now knows a new order, one tempered by the disciplined hand of Guilliman and the silent vigilance of the Lion. 
            No longer is the Imperium fractured by competing ambitions or stagnated by ancient dogma.
            Together, they rule--not as separate figures, but as a unified force, their leadership indivisible and absolute. 
            The Imperium is no longer a fragile construct upheld by faith alone. It is a realm of order, strength, and unparalleled resolve, where the sword and the word are one.
            The Lion demands not worship, but obedience, and Guilliman commands not through divine right, but through purpose and strategy. 
            Their combined reign is not one of hope or faith, but of absolute control, ensuring peace through the promise of discipline and the certainty of the sword. 
            Under this new order, the Imperium shall endure--unbroken, unyielding, and eternal.
            The Age of the Primarchs has begun.
            &lt;/s&gt;
        </Comment>
        <SubFunctionType Type="SubFuncType" Library="Ntve" Id="00000004"/>
