    <Element Type="Comment" Id="D0CA1A6E">
        <Comment>
            &lt;s val=&quot;AB_Description&quot;&gt;
            The stars have gone silent. Across the galaxy, the lights of civilization have been extinguished, one by one, beneath the claws and tendrils of Hive Fleets Kraken and Leviathan. 
            What began as a scattered invasion became an unstoppable tide--Kraken striking swift and surgically, tearing through defenses before they could form; 
            Leviathan following close behind, adapting, absorbing, perfecting. Together, they evolved faster than the galaxy could resist.
            The Imperium is no more. The Necrons lie dismantled, their cold machinery torn apart and repurposed as biomass. 
            The Tau Empire fell in silence, their innovations devoured. Chaos, unable to corrupt what feels no fear, has withered in the warp, its gods starved of sensation. 
            Even Jormungandr, the slow and methodical brother-fleet, was overrun--its role made obsolete by the precision and efficiency of Kraken and Leviathan combined.
            No alliances. No diplomacy. No negotiation. Just hunger.
            With nothing left to resist them, Leviathan spreads through the galactic core, adapting endlessly. 
            Kraken coils outward in fractal patterns, stripping worlds before their echoes can reach the next. Planets vanish. Stars are veiled. There is no longer a war. 
            There is only the feast.
            The galaxy is quiet now. It breathes no more. The Hive Mind hungers still--endlessly, perfectly, eternally.
            &lt;/s&gt;
        </Comment>
