    <Element Type="Comment" Id="4F59EE18">
        <Comment>
            &lt;s val=&quot;AB_Description&quot;&gt;
            The galaxy fell not in a blaze, but under the weight of inevitability. Hive Fleets Leviathan and Jormungandr, each a perfect instrument of the Hive Mind&apos;s will, converged upon the stars with slow, merciless certainty. 
            Leviathan adapted to every resistance, evolving faster than enemies could react. Jormungandr dug deep, anchoring the invasion beneath the very ground, its tendrils spreading unseen until escape was no longer possible.
            The Imperium crumbled, its defenses cracked open and consumed from within. 
            The Tau Empire, despite its advancement, was too small to survive the slow constriction. The Necron dynasties, unfeeling and eternal, could not adapt to the evolving tide. 
            Chaos burned bright for a moment--then was snuffed out, unable to seduce what knows no fear. Even Kraken, once the swift blade of the Hive Mind, was abandoned, deemed inefficient against this perfected strategy of strangulation and adaptation.
            Planets vanished without battle. Civilizations were buried in silence. There were no last stands--only digestion.
            Now, the galaxy is still. Leviathan&apos;s endless mutations continue to spread across the stars, while Jormungandr&apos;s coiled network chokes the void beneath. 
            The war is over. The prey is gone.
            And yet, the Hive Mind is not sated. Its hunger remains--colossal, calculating, and eternal.
            &lt;/s&gt;
        </Comment>
